   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the administrative code of the city of New York and the\nretirement and social security law, in relation to permitting certain New York\ncity correction members to borrow from their accumulated member contributions;\nand to repeal certain provisions of the retirement and social security law\nrelating thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S6416",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6416-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 17,
       "fullName": "Iwen Chu",
       "imgName": "1331_Iwen_Chu.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 1514,
       "sessionMemberId": 1877,
       "sessionYear": 2023,
       "shortName": "CHU"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Rpld §445-a sub d ¶8, §445-c sub d ¶12, §504-a sub e ¶9, §504-b sub e ¶13, amd §§445-a, 445-c & 517-c, R & SS L; amd §13-140, NYC Ad Cd",
    "lawSection": "New York City Administrative Code",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6416\n\nSPONSOR: JACKSON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the administrative code of the city of New York and the\nretirement and social security law, in relation to permitting certain\nNew York city correction members to borrow from their accumulated member\ncontributions; and to repeal certain provisions of the retirement and\nsocial security law relating thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill permits New York City correction officers to borrow from their\naccumulated member contributions.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 repeals paragraph 8 of subdivision d of Section 445-a of the\nRetirement and Social Security Law.\n\nSection 2 repeals paragraph 12 of subdivision d of section 445-c of the\nRetirement and Social Security Law.\n\nSection 3 repeals paragraph 9 of subdivision e of section 504-a of the\nRetirement and Social Security Law.\n\nSection 4 repeals paragraph 13 of subdivision e of section 504-b of the\nRetirement and Social Security Law.\n\nSection 5 amends the New York City Administrative Code Section 13-140 to\nallow members to borrow against their additional contributions that were\nmade pursuant to Retirement and Social Security Law Section 445-a or\n445-c.\n\nSection 6 amends Section 517-c of the Retirement and Social Security Law\nSection 517-c to allow members of NYSLRS, PFRS, and NYCBERS to borrow\nagainst their additional contributions that were made pursuant to\nRetirement and Social Security Law Sections 504-a or 504-b.\n\nSection 7 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is designed to provide New York City Correction offi-\ncers with the same pension and retirement benefits as other municipal\nemployees in New York State. It has long been a commonly administered\nbenefit to allow a retirement system member who has contributed to his\naccumulated benefit account to access a portion of those funds which\nhave been earned. This legislation seeks to level the playing field in\nterms of benefits and options afforded for municipal employees.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021-2022 - S.6987-B - Amend and Recommit to Civil Service and Pensions\n\n2019-2020: S.5851-A - Referred to Civil Service and Pensions/A.8180 -\nReferred to Governmental Employees\n\n2017-2018: S.6134-A - Amend and Recommit to Cities\n\n \nSTATE AND LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee fiscal note.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
